  <iati-identifier>GB-COH-1762840-KEN207-AF01-01</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-COH-1762840" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HelpAge International</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards an effective, efficient and accountable pension scheme for all persons 70years&amp;above in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(O1) ACCESS: access to the Inua Jamii 70+ programme for older women and men in project locations is more effective, appropriate and equitable. 14,000 older women and men and 6,000 designated caregivers will directly benefit from activities put in place to achieve this objective</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(O2) SOCIAL ACCOUNTABILITY: accountability of targeted stakeholders involved in the execution of the IJ70+ programme, and in particular the government of Kenya, will be strengthened including in target areas.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(O3) CAPACITY AND CAPITALISATION: targeted State and non-State actors of the social protection sector will demonstrate improved capacity to implement inclusive, integrated, age-gender-and disability-friendly programmes in Kenya thanks to the experience and evidence provided by the project.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to improve the systems and access to social protection programmes for marginalised older women and men in urban setting in Kenya. This general objective is articulated around three specific or intermediary objectives along an access-accountability-learning axis:</narrative>
  </description>
